{"title":"2018 AMC 8 Problems/Problem 16","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 1</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_1,_Detailed_Solution\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution 1, Detailed Solution</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_2_by_OmegaLearn\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution 2 by OmegaLearn</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#See_Also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">5</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See Also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2018_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_16&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Professor Chang has nine different language books lined up on a bookshelf: two Arabic, three German, and four Spanish. How many ways are there to arrange the nine books on the shelf keeping the Arabic books together and keeping the Spanish books together?\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/a/6/0a6e1f56e62b08ceb68818e2698f93e0e78aace5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(A) }1440\\qquad\\textbf{(B) }2880\\qquad\\textbf{(C) }5760\\qquad\\textbf{(D) }182,440\\qquad \\textbf{(E) }362,880$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"541\" height=\"17\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2018_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_16&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>To solve this, treat the two Arabic books as one unit and the four Spanish books as another unit. Along with the three German books, you now have five units to arrange.\n</p><p>You can arrange these five units in <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/9/3/2933f407c21ceb3f3ec8370f43cd5b939250ffca.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5!$\" width=\"12\" height=\"13\" /> ways. Within the Arabic block, the two books can be arranged in <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/8/c/08ce4ccc8f0624befaa9ce7855fc1afc69b8e5ea.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2!$\" width=\"12\" height=\"13\" /> ways, and within the Spanish block, the four books can be arranged in <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/d/a/2da866442e69c040daf44260b4728d37e98de313.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4!$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"12\" height=\"13\" /> ways.\n</p><p><br />\nSo now we try to find the german book possibilities, (Arabic block), (Spanish block), German book 1, German book 2, German book 3. 5!\n</p><p><br />\nMultiplying all these possibilities(2!,4!,5!) gives the total number of arrangements which is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/f/7/8f7a69363101f82ca3ffe771c9bde3beef6be0dd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf{(C) }5760}.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"90\" height=\"30\" /> ways to arrange the nine books while keeping the Arabic and Spanish books together.\n-TORPEDOROCKS\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Video_Solution_1.2C_Detailed_Solution\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_1,_Detailed_Solution\">Video Solution 1, Detailed Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2018_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_16&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution 1, Detailed Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=GznYT3zMh3o\">https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=GznYT3zMh3o</a>\n</p><p>~Octopus72\n</p><p>~Video provided by Education, the Study of Everything\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_2_by_OmegaLearn\">Video Solution 2 by OmegaLearn</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2018_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_16&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution 2 by OmegaLearn\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=t6a4uHEwQnM&amp;list=PLT9bNzqjDoMmMNsMAJ3g7C4ptRnPMMrpT\">https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=t6a4uHEwQnM&amp;list=PLT9bNzqjDoMmMNsMAJ3g7C4ptRnPMMrpT</a>\n</p><p>~Octopus72\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2018_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_16&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=